  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to have a shared target relationship with 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which in turn targets KALS-1. This suggests a potential pathway where Mollicellin N influences the activity of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which then modulates KALS-1. The evidence from multiple paths indicates that Mollicellin N acts as a regulator of this metabolic cascade, with varying degrees of direct interaction. The consistent presence of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid as a common intermediate across different targets supports a functional link between Mollicellin N and KALS-1. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Mollicellin N in regulating the expression or activity of KALS-1 through a metabolic intermediate.",
